{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Rule 6c-11(b) conditionally exempts eligible ETFs from four Investment Company Act requirements:\n\n1. **Affiliated transactions:** relief from §17(a)(1) and (2), allowing certain in-kind creations and redemptions with an affiliated person. It does **not** permit an ETF or affiliate to select or influence the securities included in a basket in a way that favors the affiliate, nor cover other affiliated transactions.\n2. **Joint transactions:** relief from §17(d) and Rule 17d-1 for those same in-kind transactions.\n3. **Prospectus delivery:** relief from §24(d) for secondary-market sales of ETF shares, subject to Rule 6c-11’s conditions and applicable securities-law disclosure obligations.\n4. **Delayed foreign delivery:** relief from §22(e)’s seven-day redemption-payment limit when local-market delivery is delayed by a holiday or extended customary delivery cycle. The delay must be no longer than necessary and may not exceed 15 days.\n\nThese exemptions are conditional, not blanket permission."}}
